# Pulse Sync

The Status Board reads **`.pulse/features/`** (one YAML card per feature / bug / tech-debt; `_meta.yaml` = project meta + `focus_id` + `code_roots`). Chat answers and raw product-doc edits do **not** update the board until a card is written + `generate`.

pulse lives only under `.pulse/` — it does not require any product folder layout.

**Prefer the CLI:**

```bash
.pulse/bin/pulse set --feature <id> --status partial --percent 40 --add-remaining "…"
.pulse/bin/pulse new --id <id> --name "…" --type feature|bug|tech-debt
.pulse/bin/pulse next --prompt
.pulse/bin/pulse explain
```

Edit **cards** under `.pulse/features/` (and `.pulse/cleancode/`). Do **not** edit vendored `.pulse/tools/` — refresh the engine with `pulse upgrade` from the kit.

## When you MUST sync a card

| Change | Action |
|---|---|
| Product **code** under folders listed in `_meta.code_roots` | Patch matching card |
| Product **docs** the team treats as SoT | Same — or `new --type feature` for net-new scope |
| **Bug** / **tech-debt** found | `new --type bug` / `new --type tech-debt` |

Then `.pulse/bin/pulse generate` and/or `drift`.

## Clean-code scoreboard (optional)

`.pulse/bin/pulse cleancode list|scan|fix|set --module <id>`

## Done / mocks / heal

- Chat “done” ≠ board done — update the card.
- `status: done` forbids non-empty `mocks` or `remaining`.
- Before claim done: `.pulse/bin/pulse mismatch detect`.
- Heal only when the user asks.

## Status questions

User asks status / next → `explain` / `next` — do not invent remaining/mocks from memory.
